      "id": 1,
      "text": "Sheridan was founded in 1866, incorporated in 1877, and named after Union Civil War General Philip Sheridan.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://villageofsheridan.com/history"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Early 1900s Main Street buzzed with shops, including a furniture and spark‑plug factory that once operated in Sheridan.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://villageofsheridan.com/history"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Sheridan’s historic water tower once stood as a landmark overlooking the village’s center.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sheridan%2C_Michigan"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The village was a stop on the Toledo, Saginaw and Muskegon Railway, linking it to regional trade.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sheridan%2C_Michigan"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Sheridan uniquely spans four townships—Evergreen, Bushnell, Fairplain, and Sidney—integrating land from each.",
